"""
The first board's canary, trained and run.

B20 fixed the canary's data set and its first two layers: MNIST pooled to
8 x 8; FC1 and FC2 the host's, at eight bits; FC3 trained for the tile at six;
all three trained in one run of grx930's harness.  Seed 1's network is the
canary, by a rule the owner made before any network was trained, and the
other four seeds' are reported beside it.  The stand-in every block of this
plan's section 4.2 ran had all three layers at six bits and the tile's noise
on every layer's sums as it trained.

MEASURED IN A MODEL, by grx930 (c930/doc/pta_error_model_design_note.md
section 5, "The first board's canary", 2026-10-14; `train --host 2`, and
`SHAPE=chain sim/pta_mnist.sh DIR WORK canary`).  Five networks, seeds 1 to
5, each trained from its seed's 8-bit network for eight epochs with noise of
a tenth of their rms on the last layer's sums alone.  Each is run as
pta_board_scale.py's reference networks were: the format alone; the tile as
budgeted, with its range fitted, lit, and lit and fitted; on 10,000 images
and on the first thousand, the gate's own; five draws; with one scale fixed
on a thousand held-out images.  250 runs.

DERIVED here:

  the tables         the three grx930 printed, cell for cell
  the canary         a row's figure for seed 1, a mean over its five draws
  against the        a row's figure for each network less the stand-in
  stand-in           reference network of the same seed's, each a mean over
                     the draws: the mean of the five and its standard error

HOW SURE.  Five networks, 2.8 errors for one in twenty.  The canary is one
network, and its own figures are a mean over five draws of the tile and not
over networks: the other four say how far a network trained the same way may
be from it.

WHAT THIS IS NOT.  The frozen canary: no golden tensor has been generated,
and whether FC3's declared reference is the sum before the converter or its
codes is not settled (B20).  The engines the canary's first two layers will
run on: the harness runs them as the host's, exactly, at eight bits, which is
B20's contract for them and not a GRX930 NPU's or a G100's measured output.
A chip, a drifted tile or a calibration cycle: everything
pta_board_chain.py says of itself.  A band for Gate F, which is proposed from
the frozen canary's run (B19).

Standard library only.  Run:  python3 docs/designs/pta_board_canary.py
"""
